{"name":"Sassafras Tea","hex":"#dbd8ca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sassafras","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of species Sassafras albidum of the eastern United States and Asia having mitten-shaped leaves and red, aromatic heartwood.","A tree of any species in the genus Sassafras."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sassafras"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sassafras","blocks":[{"text":"Sassafras is a genus of three extant and one extinct species of deciduous trees in the family Lauraceae, native to eastern North America and eastern Asia. The genus is distinguished by its aromatic properties, which have made the tree useful to humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sassafras_Leaves_June_Nbg_%28261691941%29.jpeg/330px-Sassafras_Leaves_June_Nbg_%28261691941%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sassafras"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi